What is a Member?

    Anything declared inside a class is called a member.

    Members can be:

        Variables (Data Members)
        Methods (Member Functions)
        Constructors
        Nested Classes


StaticBlockDemo :

    Java executed it automatically when the class was loaded into memory by the JVM

            1. JVM starts
                    ↓
            2. Class is loaded into memory
                    ↓
            3. Static variables are initialized
                    ↓
            4. Static blocks are executed
                    ↓
            5. main() method is called
                    ↓
            6. Objects are created (if you create them)
                    ↓
            7. Constructors execute
                    ↓
            8. Non-static methods execute (when called)

                    class Student {

                            static {
                                System.out.println("Student Static Block");
                            }

                            Student() {
                                System.out.println("Constructor");
                            }
                   }

                 public class Demo {

                            static {
                                System.out.println("Demo Static Block");
                            }

                            public static void main(String[] args) {

                                Student s1 = new Student();
                                Student s2 = new Student();

                            }
                 }


        output :
                Demo Static Block
                Student Static Block
                Constructor
                Constructor
